I did not add the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, and fetching that URL would need `aap:caps/http-client`, which is outside that authority. The node therefore makes no outbound request, and its output is unchanged.

The body marks each considered id as seen in the `seen` store, but only when the digest was published, so an unpublished run leaves its items to be retried. `recorded` is the number of ids written, which is never negative.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                state_rw::put(id, "seen");
                recorded += 1;
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

